{docstring Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.IsEssentiallySelfAdjoint}

An essentially self-adjoint operator has exactly one self-adjoint extension, its closure
({apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.eq_closure_of_isSelfAdjoint_of_le}[`eq_closure_of_isSelfAdjoint_of_le`]):

```lean (name := checkUniqueExt)
open Physicslib4 Spectral Unbounded in
#check existsUnique_isSelfAdjoint_extension
```

```leanOutput checkUniqueExt
Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.existsUnique_isSelfAdjoint_extension.{u_1} {H : Type u_1} [NormedAddCommGroup H]
  [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H] {T : H →ₗ.[ℂ] H} (h : IsEssentiallySelfAdjoint T) :
  ∃! B, IsSelfAdjoint B ∧ T ≤ B
```

Here `B` ranges over `H →ₗ.[ℂ] H`, and `T ≤ B` says that `B` extends `T`. The adjoint is well
defined ({apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.existsUnique_adjoint_apply}[`existsUnique_adjoint_apply`]);
a densely defined $`T` is symmetric exactly when $`T \le T^*`
({apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.isSymmetric_iff_le_adjoint}[`isSymmetric_iff_le_adjoint`]),
and then closable
({apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.isClosable_of_isSymmetric}[`isClosable_of_isSymmetric`]),
with $`(T^{\mathrm{cl}})^* = T^*`
({apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.adjoint_closure_eq_adjoint}[`adjoint_closure_eq_adjoint`]).
The sequential description of closedness is
{apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.isClosed_iff_forall_tendsto}[`isClosed_iff_forall_tendsto`],
and $`\mathrm{Range}(T)^\perp = \mathrm{Ker}(T^*)` is
{apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.orthogonal_range_eq_ker_adjoint}[`orthogonal_range_eq_ker_adjoint`],
with the kernel and range of a partial map defined as subspaces of $`H`
({apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.ker}[`ker`], {apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.range}[`range`]).
A self-adjoint operator plus a bounded self-adjoint one is self-adjoint on the same domain
({apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.isSelfAdjoint_add_of_isSelfAdjoint}[`isSelfAdjoint_add_of_isSelfAdjoint`]).

