## Direct sums

Blueprint: [lmm:finite-direct-sum-dense][ub-fds], [def:internal-orthogonal-decomposition][ub-iod],
[lmm:internal-decomposition-unitary][ub-idu], [prpstn:hall-9.26][ub-926],
[prpstn:hall-9.26-internal][ub-926i].

{docstring Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.IsDirectSumOperator}

The componentwise operator is essentially self-adjoint:

```lean (name := checkDirectSum)
open Physicslib4 Spectral Unbounded in
#check isEssentiallySelfAdjoint_of_isDirectSumOperator
```

```leanOutput checkDirectSum
Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.isEssentiallySelfAdjoint_of_isDirectSumOperator.{u_2, u_3} {ι : Type u_2}
  {G : ι → Type u_3} [(i : ι) → NormedAddCommGroup (G i)] [(i : ι) → InnerProductSpace ℂ (G i)]
  [∀ (i : ι), CompleteSpace (G i)] {A : (i : ι) → G i →L[ℂ] G i} {T : ↥(lp G 2) →ₗ.[ℂ] ↥(lp G 2)}
  (hA : ∀ (i : ι), IsSelfAdjoint (A i)) (hT : IsDirectSumOperator A T) : IsEssentiallySelfAdjoint T
```

Its closure and its adjoint have the maximal domain
{apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.directSumDomain}[`directSumDomain`]
({apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.domain_closure_eq_directSumDomain}[`domain_closure_eq_directSumDomain`]).
The internal form, for an
{apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.IsInternalOrthogonalDecomposition}[`IsInternalOrthogonalDecomposition`]
of $`H` into closed subspaces, is
{apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.isEssentiallySelfAdjoint_of_isInternalDirectSumOperator}[`isEssentiallySelfAdjoint_of_isInternalDirectSumOperator`];
such a decomposition makes $`H` unitarily the external direct sum of its summands
({apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.isHilbertSum_of_isInternalOrthogonalDecomposition}[`isHilbertSum_of_isInternalOrthogonalDecomposition`],
in Mathlib's language of `IsHilbertSum`).

