## Integration against a projection-valued measure

Blueprint: [def:hall-quadratic-form-on-a-subspace][ub-qf], [prpstn:hall-10.2][ub-102],
[prpstn:hall-10.1][ub-101], [prpstn:coincidence-with-the-bounded-integral][ub-coin],
[lmm:truncations-converge][ub-trunc], [prpstn:hall-10.3][ub-103].

{docstring Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.integralDomain}

{docstring Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.integralApply}

{docstring Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.pmapIntegral}

The integral is determined by its expectation values: an operator with domain $`W_f` and
$`\langle \psi, A\psi \rangle = \int f \, d\mu_\psi` is $`\int f \, d\mu`
({apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.eq_pmapIntegral_of_inner_self}[`eq_pmapIntegral_of_inner_self`]).
For bounded measurable $`f` it is the bounded integral, defined on all of $`H`:

```lean (name := checkBddIntegral)
open Physicslib4 Spectral Unbounded in
#check pmapIntegral_of_bddMeasurable
```

```leanOutput checkBddIntegral
Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.pmapIntegral_of_bddMeasurable.{u_1, u_2} {X : Type u_1} [MeasurableSpace X]
  {H : Type u_2} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H] (μ : ProjectionValuedMeasure X H)
  {f : X → ℂ} (hf : f ∈ BddMeasurable X) : pmapIntegral μ f = (↑(μ.integral f)).toPMap ⊤
```

The headline result of the subsection, the self-adjointness of $`\int f \, d\mu` for real $`f`,
proved without direct sums (see {ref "unbounded-design"}[Design]):

```lean (name := checkIntegralSA)
open Physicslib4 Spectral Unbounded in
#check isSelfAdjoint_pmapIntegral_of_real
```

```leanOutput checkIntegralSA
Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.isSelfAdjoint_pmapIntegral_of_real.{u_1, u_2} {X : Type u_1} [MeasurableSpace X]
  {H : Type u_2} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H] (μ : ProjectionValuedMeasure X H)
  {f : X → ℂ} (hf : Measurable f) (hreal : ∀ (x : X), (f x).im = 0) : IsSelfAdjoint (pmapIntegral μ f)
```

The density of $`W_f` is
{apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.dense_integralDomain}[`dense_integralDomain`], the
representation of the polarization of $`Q_f`
{apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.existsUnique_repr_integralForm}[`existsUnique_repr_integralForm`],
and the forms on a subspace are
{apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.IsQuadraticFormOn}[`IsQuadraticFormOn`] and
{apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.IsBoundedQuadraticFormOn}[`IsBoundedQuadraticFormOn`].
The truncations $`f \cdot 1_{|f| < n}` give $`(\int f \, d\mu)\psi` as a limit of bounded integrals
({apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.tendsto_integral_truncation}[`tendsto_integral_truncation`]).

