## The Cayley transform

Blueprint: [lmm:unitary-is-normal][ub-unn], [lmm:cayley-map][ub-cm], [thrm:hall-10.28][ub-1028],
[lmm:cayley-spectral-mapping][ub-csm], [lmm:borel-bijection-transports-pvm][ub-bbt],
[lmm:cayley-omits-one][ub-c1], [prpstn:hall-10.29][ub-1029], [thrm:hall-10.30][ub-1030].

{docstring Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.cayleyMap}

{docstring Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.IsCayleyTransform}

The existence theorem
{apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.exists_isCayleyTransform}[`exists_isCayleyTransform`] gives,
besides `IsCayleyTransform A B U`: $`U` is unitary, $`U - \mathbf{1}` is injective with
range $`\mathrm{Dom}(A)`, $`A(U - \mathbf{1})\chi = i(U + \mathbf{1})\chi`, and
$`U - \mathbf{1} = 2iB`. The Cayley map sends $`\sigma(A)` onto $`\sigma(U) \setminus \{1\}`
({apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.mem_spectrum_iff_cayleyMap_mem_spectrum}[`mem_spectrum_iff_cayleyMap_mem_spectrum`],
{apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.cayleyMap_image_spectrum}[`cayleyMap_image_spectrum`]),
the spectral measure of $`U` gives no mass to $`1`
({apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.spectralMeasure_singleton_one_eq_zero}[`spectralMeasure_singleton_one_eq_zero`]),
and $`A = \int D \, d\mu^U`
({apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.pmapIntegral_cayleyInv_eq}[`pmapIntegral_cayleyInv_eq`],
with $`D` the function {apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.cayleyInv}[`cayleyInv`]).

{docstring Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.cayleyPVM}

The existence half of the spectral theorem:

```lean (name := checkCayleyPVM)
open Physicslib4 Spectral Unbounded in
#check pmapIntegral_cayleyPVM_id
```

```leanOutput checkCayleyPVM
Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.pmapIntegral_cayleyPVM_id.{u_1} {H : Type u_1} [NormedAddCommGroup H]
  [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H] [Nontrivial H] {A : H →ₗ.[ℂ] H} (hA : IsSelfAdjoint A) {B U : H →L[ℂ] H}
  (hU : IsCayleyTransform A B U) {μU : ProjectionValuedMeasure (↑(spectrum ℂ U)) H}
  (hμU : (μU.integral fun u => ↑u) = U) : (pmapIntegral (cayleyPVM μU) fun x => ↑x) = A
```

The blueprint's restriction and transport of projection-valued measures are
{apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.restrictPVM}[`restrictPVM`] and
{apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.mapPVM}[`mapPVM`]; the pushforward used for uniqueness is
{apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.pushforwardPVM}[`pushforwardPVM`].

