## The spectral theorem and the functional calculus

Blueprint: [thrm:hall-10.4][ub-104], [def:spectral-measure][ub-sm], [def:hall-10.5][ub-105],
[lmm:functional-calculus-bounded][ub-fcb].

The headline theorem of the section:

```lean (name := checkSpectral)
open Physicslib4 Spectral Unbounded in
#check existsUnique_spectralMeasure_unbounded
```

```leanOutput checkSpectral
Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.existsUnique_spectralMeasure_unbounded.{u_1} {H : Type u_1} [NormedAddCommGroup H]
  [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H] {A : H →ₗ.[ℂ] H} (hA : IsSelfAdjoint A) :
  ∃! μ, (pmapIntegral μ fun x => ↑x) = A
```

Here `μ` ranges over `ProjectionValuedMeasure ℝ H`. The equation is between partial maps, so it
includes $`\mathrm{Dom}(A) = W_\lambda`, the vectors with $`\int \lambda^2 \, d\mu_\psi < \infty`
({apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.domain_eq_integralDomain_spectralMeasure}[`domain_eq_integralDomain_spectralMeasure`]).
The measure is concentrated on the spectrum:

```lean (name := checkConcentrated)
open Physicslib4 Spectral Unbounded in
#check spectralMeasure_concentrated
```

```leanOutput checkConcentrated
Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.spectralMeasure_concentrated.{u_1} {H : Type u_1} [NormedAddCommGroup H]
  [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H] {A : H →ₗ.[ℂ] H} (hA : IsSelfAdjoint A) {μ : ProjectionValuedMeasure ℝ H}
  (hμ : (pmapIntegral μ fun x => ↑x) = A) :
  μ {x | ↑x ∉ pmapSpectrum A} = 0 ∧ ∀ (E : Set ℝ), MeasurableSet E → μ E = μ (E ∩ {x | ↑x ∈ pmapSpectrum A})
```

{docstring Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.spectralMeasure}

{docstring Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.functionalCalculus}

Since $`f(A)` is by definition `pmapIntegral` for the spectral measure, the theorems of the
integration subsection apply to it: for example, $`f(A)` is self-adjoint for real measurable
$`f` by {apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.isSelfAdjoint_pmapIntegral_of_real}[`isSelfAdjoint_pmapIntegral_of_real`]. For bounded measurable $`f`, $`f(A)` is bounded
and defined everywhere. The prefix `Unbounded.` below distinguishes the declarations from their
bounded namesakes of the {ref "spectral"}[bounded chapter]:

```lean (name := checkBddCalc)
open Physicslib4 Spectral Unbounded in
#check functionalCalculus_of_bddMeasurable
```

```leanOutput checkBddCalc
Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.functionalCalculus_of_bddMeasurable.{u_1} {H : Type u_1} [NormedAddCommGroup H]
  [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H] {A : H →ₗ.[ℂ] H} (hA : IsSelfAdjoint A) {f : ℝ → ℂ}
  (hf : f ∈ BddMeasurable ℝ) :
  (Unbounded.functionalCalculus hA f).domain = ⊤ ∧
    Unbounded.functionalCalculus hA f = (↑((Unbounded.spectralMeasure hA).integral f)).toPMap ⊤
```

The unitary group $`e^{itA}` of Stone's theorem is of this kind.

