# Where to look
%%%
tag := "unbounded-files"
%%%

The section is formalised in `Physicslib4/Spectral/Unbounded/`, in eight files, by topic. Each entry links
to the API documentation of a representative declaration, from which the rest of the file can be
browsed.

* `Basic.lean`: dense domains, the adjoint, symmetric, positive and essentially self-adjoint
  operators, closures, kernels and ranges, and $`T - \lambda\mathbf{1}`,
  {apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.IsEssentiallySelfAdjoint}[`IsEssentiallySelfAdjoint`].
* `Spectrum.lean`: the resolvent set and the spectrum, the reality of the spectrum of a self-adjoint
  operator, and the criterion for essential self-adjointness,
  {apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.pmapSpectrum_subset_real}[`pmapSpectrum_subset_real`].
* `DirectSum.lean`: internal orthogonal decompositions and componentwise operators on direct sums,
  {apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.isEssentiallySelfAdjoint_of_isDirectSumOperator}[`isEssentiallySelfAdjoint_of_isDirectSumOperator`].
* `Integral.lean`: forms on a subspace and the integral of an unbounded function,
  {apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.pmapIntegral}[`pmapIntegral`].
* `Normal.lean`: polynomials in $`A` and $`A^*`, spectral subspaces, almost eigenvectors and the
  continuous functional calculus of a bounded normal operator,
  {apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.normalCalculus}[`normalCalculus`].
* `AbstractCalculus.lean`: the projection-valued measure of an abstract continuous functional
  calculus and the spectral theorem for bounded normal operators,
  {apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.existsUnique_spectralMeasure_normal}[`existsUnique_spectralMeasure_normal`].
* `Cayley.lean`: the Cayley map and transform, the transport of projection-valued measures, and the
  spectral theorem for unbounded self-adjoint operators,
  {apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.existsUnique_spectralMeasure_unbounded}[`existsUnique_spectralMeasure_unbounded`].
* `FunctionalCalculus.lean`: the spectral measure and the functional calculus of an unbounded
  self-adjoint operator,
  {apiDocs Physicslib4.Spectral.Unbounded.functionalCalculus}[`functionalCalculus`].

The bounded theory these files build on is in the top-level files of `Physicslib4/Spectral/`,
described in the {ref "spectral-files"}[bounded chapter]. The blueprint section is
[Section 10.3](https://physicslib.github.io/physicslib4/blueprint/chptr-haag-kastler-axioms-blueprint.html#sctn:unbounded-spectral-theorems),
and each entry there links to the Lean declarations that formalise it.
